      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "More info added:\n\nthis happens to standalone Quest. Also on Quest 2 PCVR+Virtual Desktop. Also Quest2 PCVR+ALVR. It only stops working after there's been a change; avi switch, avi reset, or maybe world change. Which might be why the below user believes this to be an isolated case.\n\nMany others have complained about this on the Discord.\n\nsteps to reproduce:\n\nstart VRC with only one controller active.\n\nOne-handed movement should be auto-enabled.\n\nIf not, enable it. Switch avatar, reset avatar, or turn osc on/off (might need an IDP change).\n\nShould be reproduced and now one-handed movement is turned off.\n\nTurning one-handed movement on and off does not restore it.\n\nResetting cache does neither.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
